{
  "comment": "Why: the blood sectors are the dungeon's slaughterhouse, so the table leans on the undead and the demon court, and it is a hunting ground: a roll bonus of one makes encounters a little more frequent and a budget scale of 1.1 makes them a little larger. Noise (blood is noise) pulls bats and brutes; the dark brings the slow bone-walkers.",
